  "published": "2026-07-31T02:06:30.45Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.9: remediation of an audit of a CONSUMER application (not an internal review) — every item started as a workaround written against this library. Behavior change: impersonation now expires (MyIdentity:Authentication:MaxImpersonationMinutes, default 60), enforced per-request on the cookie and periodically on the Blazor circuit; an impersonation cookie minted by alpha.8 carries no start stamp and counts as EXPIRED on first validation (fail closed) — set 0 to restore the previous behavior. IMyIdentityConfigurationService gained MaxImpersonationMinutes() with no default implementation (source-breaking only for a hand-rolled implementation). Breaking: SignInAfterRegister/ThirdPartyAuthenticator/EmailVerifiedByProvider were removed from MyIdentityRegisterDTO, where [FromBody] binding made them settable by any anonymous caller; server-side external-provider integrations move to the 5-argument RegisterAsync overload taking MyIdentityExternalRegistration (a non-null instance also creates the account WITHOUT a local password). Added: MyIdentity:Authentication:DataProtection:KeyProtection (Auto/DpapiCurrentUser/DpapiLocalMachine/Certificate/None — Auto is the default and reproduces the previous behavior exactly); the optional IMyIdentityScopeValidator seam; MyIdentityUserService.EnsureCallerCanManageAsync is protected virtual and OnBeforeUpdateAsync is new; GetUsersAffectedByRoleAsync returns MyIdentityAffectedUser (GetUserIdsAffectedByRoleAsync kept, delegating); OnBeforePermissionsRemovedAsync. See UPGRADE.md §22 for the full changelog and migration steps. API may still change before stable.",
